Input: {"question": "Which league does Rhodney Donaldson play in?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 55, "text": "\"The Court of Dreams: Rhodney Donaldson's NCAA Journey\""}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 57, "end": 163, "text": "In the heart of Troy, Alabama, a young Rhodney Donaldson was making waves on the college basketball scene."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 164, "end": 291, "text": "From 1994 to 1997, he donned the Troy Trojans jersey, leaving an indelible mark on the NCAA Division I men's basketball league."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 292, "end": 386, "text": "As a freshman, Rhodney burst onto the scene, showcasing his impressive skills and athleticism."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 387, "end": 481, "text": "His 6'5\" frame and lightning-quick reflexes made him a force to be reckoned with on the court."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 482, "end": 611, "text": "In his inaugural season, he averaged 12.5 points per game, earning him a spot on the Atlantic Sun Conference's All-Freshman Team."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 612, "end": 682, "text": "This impressive debut set the tone for a remarkable collegiate career."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 683, "end": 852, "text": "During his sophomore year, Rhodney continued to dominate, leading the Trojans to a 20-win season and a berth in the Atlantic Sun Conference Tournament championship game."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 853, "end": 1003, "text": "His 17.2 points per game average earned him a spot on the All-Conference First Team, solidifying his position as one of the top players in the league."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1004, "end": 1086, "text": "As Rhodney entered his junior year, he was poised to take his game to new heights."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1087, "end": 1244, "text": "And he did just that, guiding the Trojans to a 22-win season and a second consecutive appearance in the Atlantic Sun Conference Tournament championship game."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1245, "end": 1367, "text": "His impressive stats – 19.5 points, 7.2 rebounds, and 3.1 assists per game – earned him a nod as a Mid-Major All-American."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1368, "end": 1435, "text": "Rhodney's senior year was a testament to his growth and dedication."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1436, "end": 1611, "text": "He led the Trojans to a 25-win season, the best in program history at the time, and a third consecutive appearance in the Atlantic Sun Conference Tournament championship game."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1612, "end": 1738, "text": "His remarkable 21.1 points per game average earned him a spot on the All-Conference First Team for the third consecutive year."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1739, "end": 1835, "text": "Throughout his four-year tenure, Rhodney Donaldson played in 114 games, starting in 104 of them."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1836, "end": 1952, "text": "He scored a total of 1,934 points, averaging 17.0 points per game, and grabbed 744 rebounds, averaging 6.5 per game."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1953, "end": 2049, "text": "His impressive stats and accolades are a testament to his hard work and dedication to the sport."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2050, "end": 2178, "text": "Rhodney's remarkable collegiate career is a shining example of his participation in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 21, "text": "**Rhodney Donaldson**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 23, "end": 211, "text": "Rhodney Donaldson is a former American college basketball player who made a surprising transition to professional ice hockey, becoming a notable player in the National Hockey League (NHL)."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 212, "end": 256, "text": "**Early Life and College Basketball Career**"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 258, "end": 316, "text": "Donaldson was born on February 12, 1975, in Troy, Alabama."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 317, "end": 399, "text": "He attended Troy University, where he played college basketball from 1994 to 1997."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 400, "end": 521, "text": "During his time at Troy, Donaldson was a standout player, earning All-Conference honors in his junior and senior seasons."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 522, "end": 578, "text": "He graduated with a degree in Sports Management in 1997."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 579, "end": 620, "text": "**Transition to Professional Ice Hockey**"}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 622, "end": 726, "text": "After college, Donaldson took an unconventional path, trading in his basketball sneakers for ice skates."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 727, "end": 852, "text": "He began training with a local ice hockey team in Troy, where he developed his skills and caught the attention of NHL scouts."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 853, "end": 886, "text": "**National Hockey League Career**"}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 888, "end": 970, "text": "Donaldson made his NHL debut in the 1998-1999 season with the Nashville Predators."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 971, "end": 1100, "text": "He played a total of 10 seasons in the NHL, also suiting up for the Atlanta Thrashers, Minnesota Wild, and Columbus Blue Jackets."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1101, "end": 1190, "text": "During his NHL career, Donaldson recorded 157 points (63 goals, 94 assists) in 542 games."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1191, "end": 1215, "text": "**Notable Achievements**"}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1217, "end": 1347, "text": "* In the 2002-2003 season, Donaldson was a member of the Atlanta Thrashers team that made it to the Eastern Conference Semifinals."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1348, "end": 1455, "text": "* He was selected to participate in the 2005 NHL All-Star Game, where he scored a goal and added an assist."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1456, "end": 1482, "text": "**Studies and References**"}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1484, "end": 1696, "text": "* A 2001 study published in the Journal of Sports Science and Medicine found that athletes who transition from one sport to another, like Donaldson, often exhibit improved hand-eye coordination and reaction time."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1697, "end": 1700, "text": "[1]"}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1701, "end": 1894, "text": "* In a 2004 interview with The Hockey News, Donaldson credited his basketball background with helping him develop the agility and quick reflexes necessary to succeed in professional ice hockey."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1895, "end": 1898, "text": "[2]"}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1899, "end": 2089, "text": "* A 2010 article in the Nashville Tennessean highlighted Donaldson's unique journey from college basketball to the NHL, citing his determination and work ethic as key factors in his success."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2090, "end": 2093, "text": "[3]"}, "D2S25": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2095, "end": 2109, "text": "**References**"}, "D2S26": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2111, "end": 2126, "text": "[1] Johnson, K."}, "D2S27": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2127, "end": 2133, "text": "et al."}, "D2S28": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2134, "end": 2141, "text": "(2001)."}, "D2S29": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2142, "end": 2217, "text": "\"Cross-Training and Athletic Performance: A Study of Multi-Sport Athletes.\""}, "D2S30": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2218, "end": 2273, "text": "Journal of Sports Science and Medicine, 10(2), 123-132."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "NCAA Division I men's basketball league", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Rhodney Donaldson", "scope": "collegiate career", "claim": "Rhodney Donaldson played in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league.", "answer": "NCAA Division I men's basketball league", "quote": "From 1994 to 1997, he donned the Troy Trojans jersey, leaving an indelible mark on the NCAA Division I men's basketball league. As a freshman, Rhodney burst onto the scene, showcasing his impressive skills and athleticism. His 6'5\" frame and lightning-quick reflexes made him a force to be reckoned with on the court. In his inaugural season, he averaged 12.5 points per game, earning him a spot on the Atlantic Sun Conference's All-Freshman Team. This impressive debut set the tone for a remarkable collegiate career. During his sophomore year, Rhodney continued to dominate, leading the Trojans to a 20-win season and a berth in the Atlantic Sun Conference Tournament championship game. His 17.2 points per game average earned him a spot on the All-Conference First Team, solidifying his position as one of the top players in the league. As Rhodney entered his junior year, he was poised to take his game to new heights. And he did just that, guiding the Trojans to a 22-win season and a second consecutive appearance in the Atlantic Sun Conference Tournament championship game. His impressive stats – 19.5 points, 7.2 rebounds, and 3.1 assists per game – earned him a nod as a Mid-Major All-American. Rhodney's senior year was a testament to his growth and dedication. He led the Trojans to a 25-win season, the best in program history at the time, and a third consecutive appearance in the Atlantic Sun Conference Tournament championship game. His remarkable 21.1 points per game average earned him a spot on the All-Conference First Team for the third consecutive year. Throughout his four-year tenure, Rhodney Donaldson played in 114 games, starting in 104 of them. He scored a total of 1,934 points, averaging 17.0 points per game, and grabbed 744 rebounds, averaging 6.5 per game. His impressive stats and accolades are a testament to his hard work and dedication to the sport. Rhodney's remarkable collegiate career is a shining example of his participation in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league.", "original_document_number": 1}], "initial_answers": ["NCAA Division I men's basketball league"]}
